ational-relay.jpg","c":"The 10th change-over on Leicester's 'K' track, and Adrian Major sends off Gerry North in hot pursuit of Bullivant.","id":"B166-10","w":"June 1968"},{"f":"crops/B167/B167-p17-adrian-major-mile.jpg","c":"CENTRE LEFT: Adrian Major (1) on the way to 2nd place in the 1 mile (4:15.2)","id":"B167-30","w":"September 1968"},{"f":"crops/B170/B170-p08-fairclough-major-changeover.jpg","c":"LEFT: Tony Fairclough completes our fastest short stage to send Adrian Major away.","id":"B170-11","w":"June 1969"},{"f":"crops/B170/B170-p33-national-league-action.jpg","c":"PHOTO ACTION AT NATIONAL LEAGUE. TOP LEFT: Dick Piotrowski heads for a ducking in the S/chase, but surfaced to go on to finish 3rd. in 9:30.8 TOP RIGHT: In the 'B' S/chase Alan Black sets the pace and also secured 3rd. position. BOTTOM LEFT: Adrian Major runs at the shoulder of Don Faircloth (Croydon) in the 'A' 5000 metres before he too finished 3rd. BOTTOM RIGHT: In the 'B' 5000 metres Laurie O'Hara proved too good for most of the second strings and he is seen here finishing 2nd.","id":"B170-56","w":"June 1969"},{"f":"crops/B170/B170-p40-adrian-major-back-cover.jpg","c":"\"PHEW! - CAN'T SAY I ENJOYED THAT!\" Ron Linstead's camera catches ADRIAN MAJOR recovering and ruminating, moments after one of his many track races.","id":"B170-66","w":"June 1969"},{"f":"crops/B171/B171-p22-sward-team-race-winners.jpg","c":"SWARD TEAM RACE WINNERS\nAdrian Major,Laurie O'Hara,John Bicourt,Peter Morris","id":"B171-36","w":"September 1969"},{"f":"crops/B175/B175-p23-adrian-major-league-5000m.jpg","c":"ADRIAN MAJOR (right) on his way to second place in the 'B' string 5,000 metres at the final league match on Aug. 22nd.","id":"B175-27","w":"September 1970"},{"f":"crops/B224/B224-p43-flashback-1970-surrey-xc.jpg","c":"January 3rd 1970 at Milford Heath and no. 80, Bob Holt (Hercules Wimbledon), leads the Surrey Senior Cross Country Championships from no. 13, Gerry North (Belgrave). Bob eventually won with Gerry runner up and Dave Holt, pictured behind Bob, 3rd. Also to be seen are Chris Wade of Ranelagh (brother of tennis star Virginia), no. 11 Adrian Major (Belgrave) who placed 5th, no. 77, Mick Fuller (Hercules Wimbledon) and we can just spot Bob Gevers (SLH). Hercules Wimbledon won the team race from Mitcham with the Bels. 3rd.","id":"B224-118","w":"June 1996"},{"f":"crops/B226/B226-p06-xc-championship-1968.jpg","c":"Lionel leads Bob Smith, Dick Piotrowski, and Adrian Major during the Belgrave 7½ miles Cross Country Championship of 1968 but all four had to give way to Tony Fairclough (1st), Laurie O'Hara (2nd) and Pat O'Connor (3rd) by the finish. The field was 36 strong.","id":"B226-12","w":"March 1998"},{"f":"crops/B229/B229-p09-team-1967-frank-jarvis.jpg","c":"Left: Part of the Belgrave T&F Team of '67 pose with President Frank Jarvis at the end of a successful season.\nBack row: Brian King (throws), Chris Keavey (middle distance), Bill Couzens (throws), Don McLean (middle-distance and steeplechase), Frank Jarvis, Nick Head (javelin), Bob Taylor (Team Manager), Bill Dance (middle distance), Adrian Major (middle distance), Alan Black (middle-distance and steeplechase).\nFront: John Mitchell (long jump and sprints), Phil Smith sprints John Martin (throws), Tony Brooks (440/880), Alan Mead 440/880).","id":"B229-18","w":"February 2001"}],"photo":{"file":"crops/B153/B153-p19-adrian-major-leads-church.jpg","caption":"TOP LEFT: Adrian Major (55) leads Church (Walton).","source":"B153-31","when":"April 1964"},"slarchive":"https://slarchive.org/#athlete/adrian-major","slRaces":16,"x":1,"legend":false}